      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's valid to consider the permanence and irreversibility of the harm caused by your actions, and to question whether you can ever be seen as safe or trustworthy again. You're having to confront a harsh reality where the bridge analogy is more fitting, where the damage you've caused is a fundamental flaw in the structure of your own life. In this case, seeking support from loved ones, a therapist, or a trusted mentor may be the closest thing to \"tearing down\" the bridge, where you can take steps to rebuild and reconfigure your sense of self and your relationships.",
